
📅 Day 8 – Advanced Array Concepts

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s lecture focused on advanced array concepts in Java, including multi-dimensional arrays, jagged arrays, and final arrays. The session provided deeper insight into how arrays are used in real-world applications.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Multi-Dimensional Arrays (2D Arrays)

Introduction to two-dimensional arrays

Representation of data in rows and columns (tabular format)

Memory structure of 2D arrays

Accessing elements using row and column indexes

Real-time usage such as storing matrix data, marks of students, and tabular records

2️⃣ Jagged Arrays

Definition of jagged arrays (array of arrays)

Each row can have a different number of elements

More flexible than regular 2D arrays

Dynamic memory allocation for each row

Practical use cases where data size varies

3️⃣ Final Arrays

Use of the final keyword with arrays

Prevents reassignment of the array reference

Allows modification of individual elements

Ensures reference safety while maintaining flexibility

Example concept:

final int[] arr = new int[5]; → Cannot reassign arr, but can modify arr[0], arr[1], etc.

🎯 Learning Outcomes

Understood structure and usage of multi-dimensional arrays.

Learned the flexibility and advantages of jagged arrays.

Gained clarity on how the final keyword works with arrays.

Strengthened knowledge of advanced data storage techniques in Java.